{"id": "EUVD-2026-67526", "enisaUuid": "26d14ae8-a218-3259-82ab-d196182fe0b0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: atomisp: gc2235: fix UAF and memory leak\n\ngc2235_probe() handles its error paths incorrectly.\n\nIf media_entity_pads_init() fails, gc2235_remove() is called, which\ntears down the subdev and frees dev, but then still falls through to\natomisp_register_i2c_module(). This results in use-after-free.\n\nIf atomisp_register_i2c_module() fails, the media entity and control\nhandler are left initialized and dev is leaked.\n\ngc2235_remove() unconditionally calls media_entity_cleanup() and\nv4l2_ctrl_handler_free(), but these are not initialized at every\nerror path in gc2235_probe().\n\nReplace gc2235_remove() calls in the probe error paths with explicit\nunwind labels that free only the resources initialized at each point\nof failure, in reverse order of initialization.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51b8dc5163d2ff2bf04019f8bf7e3bd0e75bb654", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/592a0e78ab08f6373c40912365759d8a066e7711", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdbb8e55578b4ab647fa58827a9dd8730d7f4add", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d57e67ea48e4d095052f2b14d8dd7593621f862f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f614bf0a64aa1cb7444d152a96798a6bf1d49e1f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/628f763aee0047ff44974388d6f70f75a763026b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g5xp-8jpc-79mv", "CVE-2026-80650"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05ba03b4-d076-3e42-b9e4-6e84cfe836e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a49d25364dfb9f8a64037488a39ab1f56c5fa419 <51b8dc5163d2ff2bf04019f8bf7e3bd0e75bb654"}, {"id": "275d2648-957d-38d5-a8a0-55fd67d20566", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "2b0ad6b9-2aae-34e5-a5dc-aeff3194cdf5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ad85094b293e40e7a2f831b0311a389d952ebd5e <d57e67ea48e4d095052f2b14d8dd7593621f862f"}, {"id": "456d6404-2aad-393b-856e-7540c0ce4325", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 4.18"}, {"id": "5017db4e-c233-3674-8f3c-fce7a08a1a9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "8930cc73-0bdb-3d47-887e-5c6f0a4e4618", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ad85094b293e40e7a2f831b0311a389d952ebd5e <592a0e78ab08f6373c40912365759d8a066e7711"}, {"id": "a138067a-029f-3969-b804-d051e6334b50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b0955cf9-770c-33ad-935c-80944fa49c8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ad85094b293e40e7a2f831b0311a389d952ebd5e <fdbb8e55578b4ab647fa58827a9dd8730d7f4add"}, {"id": "b58f5610-6451-3414-a81e-452ae0cffc01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "c8ced80e-10ca-35bb-8276-fa78ab624769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "cbf51525-1757-348a-9e05-ecf24edba642", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "dce37e97-514e-38ff-9771-104c1dc145e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "ec07dd2f-4e0f-328c-9685-047d8fae31fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ad85094b293e40e7a2f831b0311a389d952ebd5e <628f763aee0047ff44974388d6f70f75a763026b"}, {"id": "fc31b8d7-6356-3aef-91a9-43479d9b0560", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ad85094b293e40e7a2f831b0311a389d952ebd5e <f614bf0a64aa1cb7444d152a967